# Current web app: configure provider, Base URL, API key and model in the AI settings UI.
# Values are stored in the browser's localStorage; this app does not load BETTER_ME_LLM_*.
# No .env file is required to start the app. Do not put real keys in this example,
# source files, or VITE_* variables: Vite can expose those values in the client build.
# Cloud inference sends relevant resume/JD text or page images directly to the chosen provider.
# Local inference requires a locally hosted service such as Ollama, configured in the UI.

# Server-side identity deployment (not VITE_*, not browser/model settings).
# Native processes use exported environment variables / the host's secret manager;
# Compose uses --env-file. See docs/deployment-auth.md for complete operator steps.
# BETTERME_AUTH_MODE=auto                 # auto preserves legacy private oidc.json; local disables only external sign-in
# BETTER_ME_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://betterme.example.com
# BETTERME_OIDC_ISSUER=https://identity.example.com
# BETTERME_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=provided-by-the-identity-administrator
# BETTERME_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=/absolute/private/client-secret
# Alternatively: BETTERME_OIDC_CONFIG=/absolute/private/oidc.json (do not mix the two sources).
# Never place real secrets in this file or upload your existing local identity database.
